{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Decision 2026-11-09 (PST, coordinator, from the operator's tags-pattern direction): releases keep the labels behavior exactly as ADR 0124 records it. A Jira-side rename of a release set from rebar leaves the rebar ticket with both names plus a BRIDGE_ALERT naming the old one, until someone removes it. Also confirmed: archived versions raise their own alert type (release-version-archived:<name>); a failed version-list read raises no alert and resolves none."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794269395535216001,"uuid":"dcf1fa5a-46ca-42a0-b880-31d2e00ee074"}